     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi All,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to build a simple hierarchical Poisson regression model. I can make it work (i.e., return reasonably narrow regression coefficient posteriors close to true values) for individual models/data, but the top-level posteriors for the regression coefficients are very wide and the means aren&#39;t at the true values. It&#39;s odd to me b/c in the simulated data (see code below) the number of observations for each model is lower than the number of individual models and, yet, the posteriors for the individual models are good while the posterior describing the top-level distribution (of regression coefficients) is bad. Any ideas?</div><div><br></div><div>Code:<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">poisHRegCode </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nimbleCode</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      A_hat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inverse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">diag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=